  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cambodia - PArTNER (Partnership for Agroecology Transition, Networking, and Efficient Resilience)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Generate economic and social changes of the Cambodian rural farmers families by improving Cambodian food market through agroecological transition and gender equity in agriculture.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Outcome is dedicated to support family farming systems by strengthening their resilience functions as food providers for the Cambodian society. The intended approach combines the increase of agricultural productivity through agroecological practices, of revenues through upgraded value-chains and the improvement of the socio-economic environment. 
Five results lead to the expected changes:
1.	Boosting ecological agriculture productivity through Farmer-to-Farmer led extension systems, processes of technical and managerial innovations and capacity training, and co-investment in agroecological production assets. Attention is given to the promotion of gender equality and pro-poor considerations in identified sectors or commodities that offer potential for benefitting women and advancing their economic empowerment, while also promoting poverty reduction.
2.	Enabling the creation of value-addition and the reach to remunerative markets by upgrading sustainable value-chains of agroecolog...(+3 characters extra in FundHub text)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Outcome targets 26.225 small-scale farmers (15.395 women) and their family members, part of clustered farmer groups for collective businesses, and members of 25 Agricultural Cooperatives at Takeo (6), Battambang (14), and Kampong Thom (5) provinces.

The Outcome is targeting the 57 members of the ALiSEA platform in Cambodia (https://ali-sea.org/) and more specifically 5 Farmer&#x2019; Organizations, 35 ACNGs, 8 private sector firms, 6 research institutions, and 2 governmental agencies.</narrative>
  </description>
